{"name":"Elf","hex":"#1b8a6b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"elf","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A supernatural being or spirit associated with illness, mischief, and harmful or dangerous magical influence; in later Norse sources, sometimes divided into benevolent light elves (inhabiting  Álfheimr) and malevolent dark elves.","A small, magical creature similar to a fairy, often mischievous, playful, or occasionally helpful."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To twist into elflocks (of hair); to mat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elf"}],"entries":[{"title":"Elf","blocks":[{"text":"An elf is a type of humanoid supernatural being in Germanic folklore. Elves appear especially in North Germanic mythology, being mentioned in the Icelandic Poetic Edda and the Prose Edda."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/%C3%84ngs%C3%A4lvor_-_Nils_Blomm%C3%A9r_1850.jpg/330px-%C3%84ngs%C3%A4lvor_-_Nils_Blomm%C3%A9r_1850.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elf","wikidata":"Q174396"},{"title":"Elf (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Elf is a 2003 American Christmas comedy film directed by Jon Favreau and written by David Berenbaum. It stars Will Ferrell as Buddy, a human raised by Santa's elves, who learns about his origins and journeys to New York City to meet his biological father. James Caan, Zooey Deschanel, Mary Steenburgen, Ed Asner and Bob Newhart appear in supporting roles."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/df/Elf_movie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elf_(film)","wikidata":"Q949879"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Phonological_development_of_the_word_elf_in_English.png/500px-Phonological_development_of_the_word_elf_in_English.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=pa